# deutsch-app — project conventions

**Source of truth: `AGENTS.md` at repo root.** Read it first — it contains the
project description, the Cursor/Claude Code division of labor, the
coordination protocol, all code conventions, and verification requirements.

Cursor-specific reminders:
- Only work from a **Tier A mission brief** in `CURSOR_TASKS.md`. Never start
  Tier B items — their architecture isn't designed yet.
- One branch per mission, named in the brief, branched from up-to-date `main`.
  Commit before stopping so the tree is clean for the next tool.
- `.husky/pre-commit` runs lint-staged + the full test suite. Never bypass it
  (`--no-verify` is forbidden). A green commit is the passing signal.
- Don't modify files outside your mission's stated file list. Flag
  out-of-scope bugs with a `// BUG:` comment instead of fixing silently.
